{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the two angels came to Sodom.</b> He calls them now angels. <b>ויתכן</b> to explain by way of the plain sense (peshat) the fact that he sometimes calls them 'men' and sometimes 'angels': when they are dispatched among human beings and involve themselves in their affairs, he refers to them in the language of 'men,' and after they completed their mission he refers to them in the language of 'angels,' for they had returned to their former station. And the way of truth I have already explained above." "<b>And Lot saw, and rose to meet them.</b> Abraham saw them from afar, for it was morning, the heat of the day, and therefore it says וירץ לקראתם. But Lot did not see them until they were close to him, for they came in the evening, as it says 'to Sodom in the evening,' and therefore it says ויקם."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:33.486564868Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}